      "note": "A slug is a mass unit, so the source's own WT converts as AERO.WT * SLUG_TO_KG = 72.96951 kg. The plan instead states 72.574 kg, which is AERO.WT * 32.0 ft/s^2 = 160 lbf over 2.2046226 lbf/kg, i.e. it assumes a standard gravity of 32.0 ft/s^2.  That figure appears nowhere in the source (G_FT_S2 = 32.174 here), so the plan is 0.54 % low.  The plan's number ships because its approved design fixes it and plan test 6 pins it verbatim in this file's header; weight, trim qbar, V and t_max_n are therefore all that much low."
